{"descriptionModels":[{"description":"Prerequisite: Dragonborn\n\nNote: This Feat is intended to use instead of the regular Dragon Hide feat.\n\nYou evolve in your body, manifesting scales, claws and strong muscles reminiscent of your draconic ancestors. You gain the following benefits:\n\n- Increase your Strength, Constitution, or Dexterity score by 1, up to a maximum of 20.\n\n- Your scales harden. While you aren\u0027t wearing armor, you can calculate your AC as 13 + your Dexterity modifier. You can use a shield and still gain this benefit. If otherwise you have a feature that grant\u0027s you a higher AC or equal AC or are wearing armor, increase your AC by 1 instead.\n\n- You can grow retractable claws from the tips of your fingers. Extending or retracting the claws requires no action. The claws are natural weapons, which you can use to make unarmed strikes. If you hit with them, you deal slashing damage equal to 1d6 + your Strength modifier, instead of the normal bludgeoning damage for an unarmed strike. Whenever you make an attack with one of those claws as part of your action, you can make another with the other one as part of the same action.","level":1}],"id":"dragon_hide","isFeature":false,"jsonType":"feat","level":1,"name":"Dragon Constitution [SM]","notes":"","type":"Feat"}